(ii) having attained the age of 14 years but being below the age of 18 years, has previously been dealt with by a court in connection with another offence and had, in respect of that other offence, been ordered under paragraph (i) to be sent to an approved school, and the Juvenile Court is satisfied that it is expedient with a view to his reformation that he should undergo a period of training in a reformative training

